{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The program does not score any top-level data variable with a sampling statement; all data variables (`N`, `ts`, `x_left`, `x_right`, `left_idxs`, `center_idxs`, and `right_idxs`) are context inputs.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only sampling statement is the built-in prior `interior_x_tildes ~ normal(0, 1)` for the top-level parameter, and there is no protected likelihood interface in this prior-only program.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  real bridge_lpdf(real x, real t, real t_left, real x_left, real t_right, real x_right) {
    real mu = x_left + (t - t_left) / (t_right - t_left) * (x_right - x_left);
    real sigma2 = (t_right - t) * (t - t_left) / (t_right - t_left);
    return normal_lpdf(x | mu, sqrt(sigma2));
  }

  real bridge_rng(real t, real t_left, real x_left, real t_right, real x_right) {
    real mu = x_left + (t - t_left) / (t_right - t_left) * (x_right - x_left);
    real sigma2 = (t_right - t) * (t - t_left) / (t_right - t_left);
    return normal_rng(mu, sqrt(sigma2));
  }
}

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real ts;

  real x_left;
  real x_right;

  array[N - 2] int left_idxs;
  array[N - 2] int center_idxs;
  array[N - 2] int right_idxs;
}

parameters {
  array[N - 2] real interior_x_tildes;
}

transformed parameters {
  array[N] real xs;

  xs[1] = x_left;
  xs[N] = x_right;

  for (n in 1:(N - 2)) {
    real t = ts[center_idxs[n]];
    real t_l = ts[left_idxs[n]];
    real x_l = xs[left_idxs[n]];
    real t_r = ts[right_idxs[n]];
    real x_r =  xs[right_idxs[n]];

    real mu = x_l + (t - t_l) / (t_r - t_l) * (x_r - x_l);
    real sigma2 = (t_r - t) * (t - t_l) / (t_r - t_l);

    xs[center_idxs[n]] = mu + sqrt(sigma2) * interior_x_tildes[n];
  }
}

model {
  interior_x_tildes ~ normal(0, 1);
}
